<Layout title="About — Shaoyun Wang"><section class="wrap page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE BACKGROUND</span><h1>About me</h1></section><section class="wrap about-grid"><aside><img class="about-portrait" src="/assets/images/IMG_018512.png" alt="Shaoyun Wang"/><h2>Shaoyun Wang</h2><p>{p.role}<br/>{p.institution}</p><a class="button" href={p.cv}>Download CV ↓</a></aside><div class="about-content"><h2>Waves, models, and experiments.</h2><p>{p.intro}</p><p>My work spans time-varying elastic media, non-Hermitian and topological physics, and computational methods. Earlier research explored piezoelectric resonators and molecular simulations of charged polymers.</p><h3>Academic appointment</h3><div class="timeline"><span>2026 —</span><div><strong>Postdoctoral Researcher</strong><p>CUNY Advanced Science Research Center · New York<br/>Advisor: Andrea Alù<br/>Research topic: Electro-momentum coupling</p></div></div><h3>Education</h3><div class="timeline"><span>Ph.D.</span><div><strong>Mechanical Engineering</strong><p>University of Missouri<br/>Dissertation: Wave propagation in elastic time-varying media</p></div></div><div class="timeline"><span>2019</span><div><strong>M.S. in Theoretical Physics</strong><p>Ningbo University</p></div></div><div class="timeline"><span>2016</span><div><strong>B.S. in Engineering Mechanics</strong><p>Ningbo University</p></div></div><h3>Selected recognition</h3><p>Second Place, ASME Noise Control and Acoustics Division Student Paper Competition, 2023.</p><h3>Get in touch</h3><p>For research conversations and potential collaborations:</p><a class="text-link" href={'mailto:'+p.email}>{p.email} ↗</a><div class="contact-links"><a href={p.scholar}>Google Scholar ↗</a><a href={p.github}>GitHub ↗</a></div></div></section></Layout>
